ine**: The slope of the line $y=-x+6$ is $-1$, so the slope of the perpendicular line is the negative reciprocal of $-1$, which is $1$.\n\n9. **Find the equation of the perpendicular line**: The equation of the perpendicular line through the origin is $y=x$.\n\n10. **Find the intersection point**: To find the intersection point of the line $y=-x+6$ and the perpendicular line $y=x$, we set the two equations equal to each other:\n\n$$-x+6=x$$\n\n$$2x=6$$\n\n$$x=3$$\n\nSubstituting $x=3$ into the equation $y=-x+6$, we get:\n\n$$y=-3+6$$\n\n$$y=3$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the point $P$ on the line $y=-x+6$ such that $P$ is closest to the origin $O(0,0)$ are $\\boxed{(3,3)}$.", "decode_seconds": 33.98778331466019, "draft_calls": 0, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 122, "method": "native_ar", "output_hash": "a1d82eaefbaf52faf857a9feaa5a1684282245b36fcf80e67bbadb4a81668820", "output_token_ids": [1271, 1505, 279, 14259, 315, 1486, 400, 47, 3, 389, 279, 1584, 400, 88, 11065, 87, 10, 21, 3, 1778, 430, 400, 47, 3, 374, 3312, 307, 11451, 505, 3585, 400, 32, 7, 605, 5106, 605, 15437, 323, 400, 46, 7, 15, 11, 15, 15437, 11, 584, 1205, 311, 1833, 1521, 7504, 1473, 16, 13, 3146, 10086, 279, 24524, 315, 279, 1584, 96618, 578, 24524, 315, 279, 1584, 374, 2736, 2728, 439, 400, 88, 11065, 87, 10, 21, 3, 382, 17, 13, 3146, 10267, 400, 47, 3, 387, 5035, 87, 7509, 15437, 96618, 8876, 400, 47, 3, 15812, 389, 279, 1584, 11, 584, 649, 28779, 400, 88, 11065, 87, 10, 21, 3, 1139, 279, 14259, 315, 400, 47, 3, 382, 18, 13, 3146, 10464, 279, 6138, 15150, 96618, 578, 6138, 1990, 1403, 3585, 5035, 87, 62, 16, 7509, 62, 16, 15437, 323, 5035, 87, 62, 17, 7509, 62, 17, 15437, 374, 2728, 555, 59060, 27986, 97165, 87, 62, 17, 6695, 62, 16, 30876, 17, 13666, 88, 62, 17, 12303, 62, 16, 30876, 17, 92, 13244, 1226, 1390, 311, 1505, 279, 1486, 400, 47, 2120, 7509, 15437, 1778, 430, 400, 8201, 28, 2089, 55976, 779, 584, 743, 709, 279, 24524, 1473, 14415, 59, 27986, 97165, 87, 12, 605, 30876,